  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.0.0 — Adds legend label styling (color, font, box size, padding, point style, text align, border radius), tooltip colors and fonts, and Ticks.Source for time scales. Fixes eighteen properties that were non-nullable value types skipped by the serializer whenever they held the type default, so 0 and false never reached Chart.js: the line and radar Fill, line and scatter Tension, ScatterDataset.ShowLine, nine DataLabels options including Offset and Opacity, the zoom drag and pan Threshold, the zoom wheel Speed, and RadarOptionsElementsLine.BorderWidth — where BorderWidth = 0 now hides the radar outline, which no value could do before. A chart that sets none of them serializes byte-for-byte as it did in 1.0.0, so nothing renders differently. Also fixes null handling across the models: nine string-enum properties threw a NullReferenceException when set to null, six properties wrote a bare null into the config instead of omitting the key, and five dataset colour lists shipped an empty [] on every untouched chart. The wrapper's internal markers (hasFilter, hasLabel, hasCustomTitle, hasCallback, hasAsyncCallback) and the crosshair, groupXAxis and groupYAxis keys no longer reach Chart.js as live options, and the legend filter no longer throws on a chart with an empty data object. Breaking: those eighteen are nullable now, so assigning is unchanged but reading one into a non-nullable local needs ?? 0 or == true; Legend.Position, Legend.TextDirection, Title.Position, Axis.Position and AxesTitle.Align are annotated nullable, which they always were at runtime; the five dataset colour lists are List<string>? with no initializer, so .Add() on one needs an instance first; Title.Padding is a TitlePadding (Top and Bottom only, which is all Chart.js reads for a title); and AxesTime.Source, Axis.Color, LineDataset.Y2AxisId, ScatterDataset.Y2AxisId, LineDataset.FillColor, LineDataset.StrokeColor and *ChartConfig.OnAnimationComplete are removed — each serialized to a key Chart.js 4 does not read, so migrating off them changes nothing on screen. Axis.Color has four replacements depending on what you meant to colour: Ticks.Color, Grid.Color, Border.Color, AxesTitle.Color. This release also adds a 284-test suite — golden-JSON snapshots for every chart type, validation of every serialized key against Chart.js's own type definitions, and a regression test per fixed defect — which CI and the publish workflow both gate on. Replacements for all of them, and the full notes, are in CHANGELOG.md: https://github.com/erkantaylan/BlazorChartjs/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
